From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 16:30:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03305/11362] [outer-loop] arc: pretrain-prior path --
 cross-game CNN prior + few-shot transfer gate + warm-start

The third of the three capture/learn components. Builds the PRETRAINED MECHANIC PRIOR the live per-game
learner warm-starts from (fewer real probe actions to converge = more 5n per-level budget left to solve).

- arc_live_ttt.CNNDynamics: mini-batched training (lazy per-batch encoding -- pre-stacking the 14.6k-corpus
  was ~5GB), get_state()/warm_state= for save+warm-start. All 25 public games are 64x64 so ONE net is a
  cross-game prior whose weights transfer directly.
- LiveTTTWorldModel(prior_state=...): _fit_l1 warm-starts the cnn backend from the prior.
- scripts/arc_pretrain_prior.py: trains the prior on the corpus (human + probes) EXCLUDING held-out games,
  then few-shot-transfer-tests warm-start vs from-scratch on the held-out games (does the prior reach
  state-changing accuracy from fewer transitions?). That few-shot gap is the faithful proxy for "adapts
  faster to a HIDDEN game" -- transfer, not memorization (the prior never trains on the held-out games).
  Saves models/arc_dynamics_prior.pt.

5 live-ttt tests green. Training run launched separately (CPU, offline). All three operator-requested
components now built: capture sink + human ingestion (committed), live-recording capture (committed),
pretrain-prior path (this).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
